# Generated OpenAPI artifacts — DELIBERATELY TRACKED, do not re-add an ignore here.
# This slot used to hold `aidis-command/frontend/.openapi/`, a path that has never
# existed under this directory (the repo was renamed to mandrel-command), so the rule
# matched nothing and only advertised an intent we do not hold. frontend/.openapi/
# openapi.json IS checked in on purpose: the frontend generates its API client from it
# and clients/customers read it as the API contract. It is kept honest by the CI gate STAGE 5o
# (scripts/test/openapi-artifact-drift.test.sh), which regenerates it from the route
# annotations and REDs on any delta. Ignoring it would silently untrack a gated artifact.

# WSL path references
\\wsl.localhost\Ubuntu\home\mandrel\aidis\aidis-command\.env.example
